                         ADDITIONAL TERMS FOR MEDICAL DEVICES

1. MEDICAL DISCLAIMER: This project is an experimental open-source medical 
   device. It has NOT been approved by any regulatory authority (e.g., NMPA, 
   FDA, CE). Use at your own risk. Always consult with a qualified healthcare 
   provider before use.

2. SAFETY REQUIREMENTS: Any derivative work MUST maintain or exceed the safety
   features documented in this project, including but not limited to:
   - Current limiting (maximum 5mA output)
   - Electrical isolation (minimum 5000V)
   - Emergency stop functionality
   - Watchdog timer protection
   - Impedance monitoring

3. PATENT GRANT: The contributors grant a worldwide, royalty-free, irrevocable
   patent license to use, make, sell, and distribute this technology for 
   medical purposes. No party may file patents that would restrict others from
   using this open-source design.

4. ATTRIBUTION: Derivative works must include the following notice:
   "Based on the Open Source Pulse Therapy Project 
    (https://github.com/scj009999/TLSR8269_SixChannel_Pulse_Generator)"

5. NON-DISCRIMINATION: This device and its derivatives may not be used to 
   discriminate against patients based on ability to pay, race, gender, 
   religion, nationality, disability, or any other protected characteristic.

================================================================================

                         NON-COMMERCIAL & VOLUNTEER TERMS

6. NON-COMMERCIAL USE: This project is STRICTLY FOR NON-COMMERCIAL USE ONLY.
   - NO ONE may use this design for commercial profit
   - NO ONE may sell this device or derivatives for profit
   - NO ONE may charge patients for treatment using this device
   - Commercial entities wishing to use this design must contact the project
     for a separate commercial license (which will include strict pricing caps)

7. VOLUNTEER BASIS: All contributors, including but not limited to doctors,
   researchers, developers, and testers, participate on a STRICTLY VOLUNTARY
   BASIS. 
   - NO compensation or payment is guaranteed or expected
   - NO employment relationship is created
   - Participants act in their personal capacity, not as representatives of
     their employers or institutions
   - The project is not responsible for any actions taken by volunteers

8. NO MEDICAL SERVICES: This project provides open-source technology ONLY.
   - We do NOT provide medical services
   - We do NOT diagnose, treat, or prescribe
   - We do NOT establish doctor-patient relationships
   - All medical decisions must be made by qualified healthcare providers

================================================================================

                         COMMITMENT TO ACCESSIBILITY

We, the contributors, pledge that:

- This design will remain open-source forever
- We will not charge royalties or licensing fees
- We will prioritize safety over cost reduction
- We will support low-resource settings and developing regions
- We will not allow commercial monopolization of this technology
- We will never charge patients for access to this technology

Every person with Parkinson's disease, regardless of economic status, deserves
access to effective treatment.

